{"skill":{"slug":"hubspot-api","displayName":"HubSpot"},"version":{"version":"1.2.9","createdAt":1790938293387,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":64235,"sha256":"28969741493c97a50a4cf220457b5d4eeb764c2bf59280e483c8f69be3af6327","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/calendly/triggers.md","size":10281,"sha256":"ae92dbfb6dd4caf628900b293d1b3c6e7d5e70cf7f6a9397407594daf50d4a48","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/github/triggers.md","size":61142,"sha256":"7424d3be38ec400eb8a4b0a6a94a94eeec40208c0bcee29a61caa5da48eea7f4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/google-mail/triggers.md","size":2648,"sha256":"5cc5065cd7db33dc33715675bbb0ee29ed49657ad9ad4354aebd1a9efdf8d8f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hubspot/triggers.md","size":8298,"sha256":"439d56e4d02e119e1de3caf79a0334243ae70c583a3e15847831c396f39c2837","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/linear/triggers.md","size":7270,"sha256":"641f6496f50e09faab921ef4c06f725122b798cb034e9f0dfaf9f838074ab377","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/notion/triggers.md","size":5840,"sha256":"fdaf3840d8213dbd7549426c1166f94cc94b09e022a1611ef2dad6f36db2f969","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/slack/triggers.md","size":6181,"sha256":"b5ee099a215223a7e5186c41a0d13fc1de68e977719304c509df105843d81f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/stripe/triggers.md","size":25651,"sha256":"ae091545396a376c7ecfe09e94b46b7bbb44fd8a72ea954bcc1239052b7959f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/time/triggers.md","size":1140,"sha256":"b8f5a523501f8d03e11e58f6426cd96b54ba0c66c8983b57c0ea31386b309e01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2188,"sha256":"3f249bba420c75bbfbd6f58cf10753b5ba782e92f786927139b8a744fe814533","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790938870048,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"22c781376d1c9fedbf619541891df13f41330a2d816151912c26c5bb10602c80","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/22c781376d1c9fedbf619541891df13f41330a2d816151912c26c5bb10602c80","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790938611839},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1790938870048},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This HubSpot skill is a disclosed Maton CLI/API integration with strong approval and least-privilege guidance for sensitive CRM operations.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, OAuth, credential-store use, and HubSpot API calls are proportionate for an API integration. The artifact warns not to inspect credentials, not to persist API keys, and to send raw HTTP keys only to api.maton.ai.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses pinned Maton CLI/package versions via npm or Homebrew, with SDK packages also pinned. No bundled executable scripts or hidden install hooks were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions repeatedly require read-first behavior and explicit user approval before connection creation, writes, deletes, hosted function deployment, trigger destinations, and local --exec handlers. The bundled HubSpot trigger reference includes ticket events, which is broader than the primary endpoint surface but is presented as event-source reference material requiring user request by name.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill can create long-lived OAuth connections, hosted functions, and persistent trigger destinations, but these are disclosed, user-approved, scoped, and include cleanup and destination-risk guidance.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is HubSpot CRM access through Maton OAuth, and the documented capabilities fit that purpose: contacts, companies, deals, associations, properties, optional hosted functions, triggers, and raw HTTP only when the CLI is unavailable.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to let Maton access your HubSpot account. Use least-privilege OAuth scopes, confirm every write/delete/bulk operation, and be especially careful with triggers or destinations because they can forward future CRM events automatically until removed.","findings":"[SDI-4] expected: The noted 'does not widen' language is somewhat imprecise because the HubSpot event catalog includes tickets, but the file clearly frames itself as reference material that configures no trigger on its own and requires the user to ask by name.\n[SDI-1] expected: Ticket trigger events are broader than the primary documented HubSpot endpoint examples, but they are HubSpot event-source metadata rather than hidden API actions; this is a documentation-scope note, not evidence of malicious or under-disclosed execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790938870048}}}}}